remove takes a bookmark's id or its name. A name in any case is enough
while only one bookmark answers to it; when two do, remove names them and
removes nothing, because this is the one thing here that cannot be undone.

Usage:
  ley bookmarks remove <id|name> [flags]

Examples:
  ley bookmarks remove "Local repeater"
  ley bookmarks remove bm_01J8Z6R9TC7QK3W4M5N6P7Q8R9

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for remove

Global Flags:
      --ascii           draw with ASCII only (no box, bar or tree glyphs)
      --color string    colour output: auto, always or never (default "auto")
      --json            machine output: proto3 JSON (NDJSON for streams)
      --socket string   daemon socket path (default: user daemon UDS, $LEYLINE_SOCKET)
